    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've been noticing that even small changes in my kitchen temp, like maybe 2-3 degrees, seem to trigger these huge spikes in acidity. It almost feels like the microbes are behaving erratically or unpredictably rather than just following a steady curve. Is there a specific threshold where the microbial community becomes unstable, or is it more about the rate of change?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
