    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's really frustrating because I feel like I'm managing everything perfectly, but then one afternoon it's just totally out of control. Like, I'll check it and it’s fine, then an hour later it’s over-fermented and smelling too sharp. Is there any way to predict these \"mood swings\" in the culture, or is the microbial activity just inherently chaotic once a certain temperature is hit?",
