      "content": "Predicting these rapid swings is challenging because microbial ecology is inherently complex and non-linear, making perfect forecasting unlikely. However, you can mitigate chaos by stabilizing your environment as much as possible, perhaps using a proofing box or consistently placing your starter near a stable heat source. Focusing on slower, more gradual feeding rates, rather than sudden environmental shocks, helps keep the microbial population in a more predictable, stable metabolic state.",
